WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.227
CREATE OR REPLACE VIEW lets you update a compatible view definition without first dropping the object.

00:00:05.227 --> 00:00:08.842
This is useful when the interface should remain available under the same name.

00:00:08.842 --> 00:00:14.692
But compatibility matters. Changing column names, meanings, types, or grain can still affect downstream users,

00:00:14.692 --> 00:00:16.122
even if the SQL command succeeds.

00:00:16.122 --> 00:00:20.327
When reading the example, do not read punctuation one character at a time.

00:00:20.327 --> 00:00:25.237
Start with the purpose of the query, then identify the input rows, the operation being applied,

00:00:25.237 --> 00:00:27.417
and the shape of the expected output.

00:00:27.417 --> 00:00:31.502
In a real setting such as an analytics team exposing a stable reporting view to dashboard users,

00:00:31.502 --> 00:00:36.597
this habit makes code reviews much easier because you can explain what the query is supposed to guarantee

00:00:36.597 --> 00:00:38.797
before discussing syntax.

00:00:38.797 --> 00:00:44.080
After running it, inspect a few records manually and check that the result matches that explanation.
